<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Singhasari</h1><p class="st-meta">1222 CE – 1292 CE · capital Tumapel (Singhasari)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The short-lived East Javanese kingdom of Ken Arok and Kertanegara, which defied Kublai Khan and paved the way for Majapahit.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ken-arok">Ken Arok</a>, a commoner turned ruler of Tumapel, overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kertajaya">Kertajaya</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kediri-kingdom">Kediri Kingdom</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ganter">Battle of Ganter</a> in 1222 and founded a new dynasty under the name Rajasa. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pararaton">Pararaton</a> chronicle tells a violent story of murders over the following generations, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wisnuwardhana">Wisnuwardhana</a> restored order in the mid-13th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its last king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kertanegara">Kertanegara</a> pursued an ambitious overseas policy: the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamalayu-expedition">Pamalayu expedition</a> of 1275 brought Sumatran <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dharmasraya">Dharmasraya</a> into his orbit, and he claimed influence over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madura">Madura</a>. He patronised a blend of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vajrayana">Tantric Buddhism</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaivism">Shaivism</a>, and his reign produced temples such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/candi-jago">Candi Jago</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/candi-singhasari">Candi Singhasari</a>. In 1289 he humiliated an envoy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1292 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayakatwang">Jayakatwang</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kediri-kingdom">Kediri</a> killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kertanegara">Kertanegara</a> and set up <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gelang-gelang">Gelang-gelang</a>. Kertanegara's son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raden-wijaya">Raden Wijaya</a> used the Mongol fleet sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> to defeat Jayakatwang in 1293, then drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> out and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/singhasari.jpg" alt="Singhasari" width="320" height="205"><figcaption>Image: Gunawan Kartapranata · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Singhasari_Kingdom_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1222 CE – 1292 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tumapel (Singhasari)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ken Arok, Wisnuwardhana, Kertanegara</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism and Tantric Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Javanese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tumapel, Singosari, Kingdom of Singhasari</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1257&amp;focus=singhasari" aria-label="Singhasari on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7794 2475 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Singhasari lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8114 2731L8112 2721M8114 2731L8097 2725M8114 2731L8272 2761M8114 2731L7816 2473M8114 2731L8186 2752"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8112 2721h0M8097 2725h0M8272 2761h0M7816 2473h0M8186 2752h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8114 2731h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8114 2731h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1257&amp;focus=singhasari">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
